{"ts": "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z", "by": "model:muse-spark", "entity": "specimen", "id": "C165", "op": "set", "field": "story", "old": "A 1973 1 krona from Sweden. The obverse shows Gustaf VI Adolf left; the reverse shows crowned arms; GUSTAF VI ADOLF SVERIGES KONUNG, 1 KRONA, date. Struck in CuNi.", "new": "A 1973 Swedish krona struck in the last year of Gustaf VI Adolf's reign — he died on 15 September 1973, and Carl XVI Gustaf took the throne. Edvin Öhrström's portrait and the crowned arms carry the king's motto 'Plikten framför allt': duty above all. The U mintmaster's mark is Benkt Ulvfot's, from the Royal Mint.", "source": "Numista N#1516 (Sweden 1 krona 1973, KM#826a, Edvin Öhrström, mintmaster U Benkt Ulvfot, motto PLIKTEN FRAMFÖR ALLT)", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "high", "provenance": {"model": "muse-spark", "prompt_version": "STORY-QUALITY-PASS@2026-10-15", "workflow": "phase2-research", "inputs": [{"file": "collection/specimens/SE.json"}], "run_id": "STORY-BATCH5-20261015"}}
